    "body": "<!--\r\n  Thanks for contributing!\r\n\r\n  Provide a description of your changes below and a general summary in the title\r\n\r\n  Please look at the following checklist to ensure that your PR can be accepted quickly:\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nThis PR uses the new method to get a single chat summary by group id and account id to remove the chat list stream subscription from the chat screen. By doing so, the use chat profile hook can be replaced by the use chat summary not only in the chat screen bun in the chat invite and chat info screens\r\n\r\n\r\n**Commit by commit:**\r\n- Moves chat summary type from chat list file in bridge to chat summary file. This because the new method to get chat summary will be used from screens that are not the chat list, so placing it in the chat list is confusing.\r\n- Adds to the bridge the new method to get a chat a single chat summary\r\n- Adds the hook to fetch chat summary from rust crate\r\n- Adds util to process how to display a chat summary (that will be used in multiple screens after)\r\n- Changes chat screen to stop subcribing to chat list and use chat summary, replacing use chat profile\r\n- Replaces  use chat profile in chat info screen by chat summary\r\n- Same for chat invite screen\r\n\r\n⚠️  With this change when a user is removed from a group it updates on navigation, If the removed user is in that chat screen when removed, it won't immediately see the warning. This is because the chat stream has no event to notify this, only the chat list had. @jgmontoya is already working on this [#806](https://github.com/marmot-protocol/whitenoise-rs/issues/806), but won't fit for thursday's release. IMO the temporary downgrade  in removal UX is not that terrible compared with the performance con of susbcribing to all chat list events on every chat when it is not really needed. But if you disaggree, then this should be  merged after we have the stream on rust side and use it here. \r\n\r\n## Type of Change\r\n\r\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- [ ] 🛠️ Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n- [ ] ❌ Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to change)\r\n- [X] 🧹 Code refactor\r\n- [ ] ✅ Build configuration change\r\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation\r\n- [ ] 🗑️ Chore\r\n- [ ] 🧪 Tests\r\n\r\n## How I Tested This\r\n- From another device, removed me from a group. Checked that once entering that chat I saw the removed warning\r\n- Blocked users logic works the same as the other PR: once I block a user, I don't see any message from that user until unblocked\r\n\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] `just precommit` passes\r\n- [ ] Related issue linked (`Closes #NNN`)\r\n- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` updated (if user-visible change)\r\n- [ ] Screenshots added (for UI changes)\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- stage-review-badge-begin -->\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://stagereview.app/marmot-protocol/whitenoise/pull/633\">\r\n  <picture>\r\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://stagereview.app/assets/gh-open-in-stage-dark.svg\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://stagereview.app/assets/gh-open-in-stage-light.svg\" alt=\"Open in Stage\">\r\n  </picture>\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n<!-- stage-review-badge-end -->",
